IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aa-types`
IMPORT `aa-act`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS — Apportionment Act 1928. Expected values were decided
-- from the source alone; see independent-expectations.md. A failing
-- assertion is a finding and is left failing.

§ `Independent tests — Apportionment Act 1928`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of payment`, st IS A `State of the payment`, amt IS A NUMBER, b IS A DATE, e IS A DATE, due IS A DATE, land IS A BOOLEAN, cap IS A BOOLEAN, pol IS A BOOLEAN, excl IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Payment
`indep payment` k st amt b e due land cap pol excl MEANS
    Payment WITH
        `kind`                                              IS k
        `a return or reimbursement of capital`              IS cap
        `an annual sum payable under a policy of assurance` IS pol
        `expressly stipulated that no apportionment shall take place` IS excl
        `state`                                             IS st
        `amount of the entire portion`                      IS amt
        `accrual period begins`                             IS b
        `accrual period ends`                               IS e
        `entire portion due on`                             IS due
        `reserved out of or charged on lands or tenements`  IS land
        `just allowances against the entire portion`        IS 0

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of payment`
GIVETH A Payment
`plain` k MEANS `indep payment` k `continuing` 36500 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

`annual rent` MEANS `plain` `rent`
`capital return` MEANS `indep payment` `dividend` `continuing` 36500 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`policy sum` MEANS `indep payment` `another periodical payment in the nature of income` `continuing` 36500 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`excluded rent` MEANS `indep payment` `rent` `continuing` 36500 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`quarter rent` MEANS `indep payment` `rent` `continuing` 900 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 2025 4 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`leap annuity` MEANS `indep payment` `annuity` `continuing` 36600 (YMD 2024 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`dividend 3650` MEANS `indep payment` `dividend` `continuing` 3650 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 31) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`salary month` MEANS `indep payment` `annuity` `continuing` 3100 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 2 1) (YMD 2025 2 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`continuing due 30 Jun` MEANS `indep payment` `rent` `continuing` 900 (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 2025 6 30) (YMD 2025 6 30) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`dead rent due 30 Jun` MEANS `indep payment` `rent` `determined by re-entry, death or otherwise` 900 (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 2025 6 30) (YMD 2025 6 30) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`dead annuity due 30 Jun` MEANS `indep payment` `annuity` `determined by re-entry, death or otherwise` 900 (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 2025 6 30) (YMD 2025 6 30) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `A — what is apportionable (ss 2, 3, 6, 7)`

#ASSERT `apportionable under the Act` `annual rent`
#ASSERT `apportionable under the Act` (`plain` `annuity`)
#ASSERT `apportionable under the Act` (`plain` `dividend`)
#ASSERT `apportionable under the Act` (`plain` `another periodical payment in the nature of income`)
#ASSERT NOT `apportionable under the Act` (`plain` `a payment that is not periodical income`)
#ASSERT NOT `apportionable under the Act` `capital return`
#ASSERT NOT `periodical income within s 3` `capital return`
#ASSERT NOT `apportionable under the Act` `policy sum`
#ASSERT NOT `apportionable under the Act` `excluded rent`
#ASSERT `the apportionment of` `capital return` `at` (YMD 2025 4 11) EQUALS `not apportionable: a return or reimbursement of capital (s 2)`
#ASSERT `the apportionment of` `policy sum` `at` (YMD 2025 4 11) EQUALS `not apportionable: an annual sum under a policy of assurance (s 6)`
#ASSERT `the apportionment of` `excluded rent` `at` (YMD 2025 4 11) EQUALS `not apportionable: apportionment expressly excluded (s 7)`
#ASSERT `the apportionment of` (`plain` `a payment that is not periodical income`) `at` (YMD 2025 4 11) EQUALS `not apportionable: not periodical income within s 3`

§§ `B — arithmetic (s 3, s 2 daily increment)`

-- B8/B1: 100 days of 365 (1 Jan -> 11 Apr 2025), 36,500 a year -> 10,000
#ASSERT `the part of` `annual rent` `accrued at` (YMD 2025 4 11) EQUALS 10000
-- B3: 0 days
#ASSERT `the part of` `annual rent` `accrued at` (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS 0
-- B4: whole period
#ASSERT `the part of` `annual rent` `accrued at` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 36500
-- B2: quarterly 900 over 90 days (1 Jan -> 1 Apr 2025), 31 Jan = 30 days -> 300
#ASSERT `the part of` `quarter rent` `accrued at` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS 300
-- B7: leap year, 366 days, 183 days run (1 Jan -> 2 Jul 2024) -> 18,300
#ASSERT `the part of` `leap annuity` `accrued at` (YMD 2024 7 2) EQUALS 18300
-- B5: dividend 3,650 over 365 days, 100 days -> 1,000
#ASSERT `the part of` `dividend 3650` `accrued at` (YMD 2025 4 11) EQUALS 1000
-- B6: salary 3,100 for 31-day January, 15 days -> 1,500
#ASSERT `the part of` `salary month` `accrued at` (YMD 2025 1 16) EQUALS 1500
-- Whole question: apportioned amount and s 4 date
#ASSERT `the apportionment of` `annual rent` `at` (YMD 2025 4 11) EQUALS `apportioned` 10000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (`the s 4 limb for` `annual rent`)
-- B9: no apportioned part under s 6 (outcome is not `apportioned`)
#ASSERT NOT `the apportionment of` `policy sum` `at` (YMD 2025 4 11) EQUALS `apportioned` 10000 (YMD 2026 1 1) (`the s 4 limb for` `policy sum`)

§§ `C — when payable (s 4)`

#ASSERT NOT `the apportioned part of` `continuing due 30 Jun` `is payable on` (YMD 2025 6 29)
#ASSERT `the apportioned part of` `continuing due 30 Jun` `is payable on` (YMD 2025 6 30)
#ASSERT `the apportioned part of` `continuing due 30 Jun` `is payable on` (YMD 2025 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the apportioned part of` `dead rent due 30 Jun` `is payable on` (YMD 2025 6 29)
#ASSERT `the apportioned part of` `dead rent due 30 Jun` `is payable on` (YMD 2025 6 30)
#ASSERT `the apportioned part of` `dead annuity due 30 Jun` `is payable on` (YMD 2025 7 1)
#ASSERT `the s 4 limb for` `continuing due 30 Jun` EQUALS "s 4(a): when the entire portion becomes due and payable, and not before"
#ASSERT `the s 4 limb for` `dead rent due 30 Jun` EQUALS "s 4(b): when the next entire portion would have been payable, and not before"

§§ `D — remedies (s 5)`

#ASSERT `s 5(1) gives remedies to` `the person entitled`
#ASSERT `s 5(1) gives remedies to` `an executor, administrator or assign of the person entitled`
#ASSERT `s 5(1) gives remedies to` `an executor, administrator or assign of a person whose interest determined with their death`
-- D4-D6: continuing land rent -> s 5(2)
#ASSERT `the route for recovering the apportioned part of` `continuing due 30 Jun` EQUALS `by suit against the person entitled to the entire rent, not against the tenant or the land`
-- D4 (R5): land rent determined by death -> s 5(2) too ("entire or continuing rent")
#ASSERT `the route for recovering the apportioned part of` `dead rent due 30 Jun` EQUALS `by suit against the person entitled to the entire rent, not against the tenant or the land`
-- D7: annuity -> s 5(1)
#ASSERT `the route for recovering the apportioned part of` `dead annuity due 30 Jun` EQUALS `the same remedies as for the entire portion`
-- rent not on land -> s 5(1)
#ASSERT `the route for recovering the apportioned part of` `annual rent` EQUALS `the same remedies as for the entire portion`
